blockOMP() => <block-omp>Current:Int</block-omp> 
when creating block of OMP, using this cell, we can create new thread with parent <>

Each blockOMP

// [o] Extract the 0 from int i=0
// [x] Extract the N from i < N


Professor, as we discussed about how to define the #pragma omp task
```
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {

    #pragma omp parallel num_threads(2)
    {
    	int n = 0;
        #pragma omp task
        {
            n=10;
            printf("Task 1, n=%d\n", n);
        }

        for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) { }
        
        #pragma omp task
        {
            printf("Task 2, n=%d\n", n);
        }

        #pragma omp taskwait
    }

    return 0;
}
```
According to our discussion we decided that 
we will set this two task as: 
blockOmpTask(_, _, int n = 0 ~> n=10 ~> printf("Task 1, n=%d\n", n))

blockOmpTask(_, _, int n = 0 ~>  for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) { } ~> printf("Task 2, n=%d\n", n))

But, due to this for-loop is executed with task 2. That is not accepted. As it is doing the same computation twice. 

Then I thought it this way, when we are creating a task we treat avaiable all variables as firstprivate to that specific task region. 
This way, we will create new storage for existing variables. and store their object location in the block-control cell. When the task will execute, 
we will take the task's associated <block-control> cell . These are propable rules for doing that: 

```
rule [copy-vars-omp-task]:
          <thread>...
               <k>
                    (.K => copyAllVars(map2List(Ids)) ~> taskStorageCreated) ~> blockOmpTask(B:K, A:K, S:K)  
               ...</k>
               <thread-local>
                    TL::Bag
                    <function-control>
                         ...
                         <block-control> 
                            <env>
                                Ids:: Map
                            </env>
                            BC::Bag
                         </block-control>
                    </function-control>
                    <block-stack>
                        .List => ListItem(<block-control> <env> Ids</env> BC </block-control>)
                    ...</block-stack>
               </thread-local>
          ...
          </thread>
          <omp-current-threads> TotalThreads:Int </omp-current-threads>
          requires TotalThreads =/=Int 0


rule [copy-individual-var-omp-task]:
          <thread>...
               <k>
                    copyAllVars(ListItem(X:CId) L:List) =>  X := OmpParentVar(X) ~> copyAllVars(L)  
               ...</k>
          ...
          </thread>

rule [copy-task-if-all-vars-are-copied]:
          <thread>...
               <k>
                    (copyAllVars(.List) => .K ) ~> taskStorageCreated ~> blockOmpTask(B:K, A:K, S:K)  
               ...</k>
               <thread-local>
                    TL::Bag
                    <function-control>
                         ...
                         <block-control> 
                            <env> Ids:: Map</env>
                            BC::Bag
                         </block-control>
                    </function-control>
               </thread-local>
          ...
          </thread>
          <next-task-id> TId:Int => TId +Int 1</next-task-id>          
          <omp-task-list>
               (.List => 
                    ListItem(
                    <omp-task>
                         <task-id> TId </task-id>
                         <task-computation> S </task-computation>
                         <task-block-control> <block-control>  <env> Ids</env>  BC</block-control> </task-block-control>
                    </omp-task>
                    )
               )
               LL:List
          </omp-task-list>


rule [enqueue-omp-task-if-multiple-threads]:
          <thread>...
               <k>
                    taskStorageCreated ~> blockOmpTask(B:K, A:K, S:K)  => .K
               ...</k>
               <thread-local>
                    TL::Bag
                    <function-control>
                         ...
                        (_:BlockControlCell => L)
                        <block-stack>
                            ListItem(L:BlockControlCell) => .List
                        ...</block-stack>     
                    </function-control>
                         </thread-local>
          ...
          </thread>
          <omp-current-threads> TotalThreads:Int </omp-current-threads>
          requires TotalThreads =/=Int 0
```

when tasks are taken from the queue, they will replace the <block-control> cell with associated task's <block-control> cell and pushed it into <block-control-stack>











     rule <k> pushLocals => .K ...</k>
          <block-control> C::Bag <local-types> LocalTypes:Set => .Set </local-types> </block-control>
          <block-stack>
               .List => ListItem(<block-control> C <local-types> LocalTypes </local-types> </block-control>)
          ...</block-stack>

     rule <k> popLocals => .K ...</k>
          (_:BlockControlCell => L)
          <block-stack>
               ListItem(L:BlockControlCell) => .List
          ...</block-stack>





